Frequently Asked Questions
What is AI-powered fall prevention in construction?

AI-powered fall prevention uses tools such as intelligent analytics, computer vision and digital safety workflows to help identify working-at-height hazards and support earlier preventive action. It supplements, rather than replaces, physical fall protection and human supervision.

Can AI detect whether construction workers are wearing safety harnesses?

Some computer-vision systems can identify visible harnesses under suitable conditions. However, recognising a harness does not prove that it is properly fitted, correctly anchored or safe for the task.

How can EHS software improve working-at-height safety?

EHS software can support hazard reporting, risk assessments, inspection records, permit management, corrective-action tracking and safety performance monitoring. These processes help improve coordination and accountability.

What is the difference between fall prevention and fall arrest?

Fall prevention aims to stop a fall from occurring, while fall-arrest systems are designed to stop a fall after it begins and limit its consequences. Suitable rescue arrangements are essential when fall-arrest equipment is used.

Can AI replace construction safety officers?

No. AI can assist with information analysis, monitoring and workflow support, but competent safety professionals remain responsible for assessing hazards, verifying controls and making safety-critical decisions.

What should construction companies prioritise when digitalising working-at-height safety?

Start with clearly defined safety procedures, effective physical controls, reliable inspections, contractor competency and corrective-action accountability. Digital tools should strengthen these established foundations.

